## Title: Adding o1-mini LLM to the extension

feat. branch #1: add @OpenAI o1-mini model to model selection, add persona-based prompt templates for summary, e.g., "Elon" persona.

## Objectives
1. Integrate @OpenAI o1-mini model as an additional selectable LLM.
2. Expand the summary feature with new prompt templates (including persona-based options, e.g., "Elon").
3. Implement flexible prompt handling so users can choose different summary types (technical, casual, "Elon," etc.).

## Context
- We already have a model selection UI using a dropdown (e.g., GPT-3.5, GPT-4). We need to add o1-mini to that list.  
- The summary component supports a default prompt; we will enhance it with multiple templates.  
- Each prompt template can be labeled and describe how to summarize the video (e.g., "Summarize as Elon Musk," "Summarize in a casual style," etc.).  

Below are the primary files where changes will take place for this update:
/add lib/constants.tsx (adding o1-mini to the model list and new persona prompts)
/add contexts/summary-context.tsx (handling new prompt and model selection logic)
/add components/summary-actions.tsx (exposing the new selection in the UI dropdown)
/add components/summary-content.tsx (ensuring any new persona prompt changes are reflected in the rendered content)

## Implementation Details
- Update the model configuration in lib/constants.tsx to include o1-mini.  
- Add persona-based prompts alongside existing prompt templates. For example:  
  - "Elon" persona: Summarize the video as if you are Elon Musk, focusing on technology, innovation, etc.  
  - "Academic" persona: Summarize with a formal, academic tone.  
  - "Casual" persona: Summarize in a friendly, conversational manner.  
- In summary-context.tsx, detect which template is selected from the new persona dropdown and include it as part of the final prompt.  
- Ensure that the new model (o1-mini) and persona-prompts are backward compatible with existing logic.  

## Constraints/Requirements
- Must fully maintain existing functionality for GPT-based models.  
- Persona prompts should be easy to configure or extend.  
- The user should see minimal performance overhead when using o1-mini.  

## Testing & Validation
- Verify that the Summary panel updates correct scripts when choosing o1-mini.  
- Validate persona prompt output in a variety of test scenarios.  
- Confirm that the user can revert to default prompts.  
- Confirm that all new calls handle errors gracefully.  

